                <pb facs="0385" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/806: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-12T23:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1928—11
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 12—9:25 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>343. Your 146, May 4, 10 [<hi rendition="#italic">5</hi>] p.m. Consul at Chefoo
                    reports Dr. Gaston categorically refuses to comply with instructions of mission
                    board. Webber suggests that board be requested to cable Gaston direct ordering
                    withdrawal.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
